    "body": "@annevk Is this still the case?\r\n\r\nI see https://drafts.csswg.org/css-viewport/#viewport-meta exists. \r\n\r\nAllowing sites to use system font size what discussed to be part of `<meta viewport>`. Per a discussion about 2.5 years ago:\r\n\r\n>Resolution from the F2F was to have a an opt-in switch for the web authors to get the true user font size, even on small screen device... Ideally the opt-in could be phased out over time if/when the Web handled scalability better.\r\n>General consensus was that this should be an addition to `<meta viewport>`\r\n\r\n_Originally posted by @cookiecrook in https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/3708#issuecomment-532113043_\r\n            \r\nI would like to continue tracking the font accessibility issue with PWA/Home Screen apps and hopefully find a resolution for Android users (Apple/Webkit has `-apple-system-body`).",
