    "body": "@clshortfuse, WebKit/Safari resolution was not to rely on -apple-system-body... Continue reading [in the same thread](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/3708#issuecomment-998406993):\r\n\r\n@ cookiecrook wrote:\r\n> The end solution was not the old -apple-system value, which is not widely used.\r\n> \r\n> The solution was that Safari added a site-specific font size control that adjusts the font for any web text, regardless of how the author specifies the units.\r\n> \r\n> <img width=\"375\" alt=\"Safari toolbar showing font size controls\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/75867/146857896-10383bb6-df93-4a8a-bc99-45b983082e06.png\">\r\n\r\n> @clshortfuse wrote:\r\n> > But Android is still forced to 16px.\r\n> \r\n> Any browser can add a font size controller to the UI. No additional spec work needed.\r\n\r\nThen the relevant zoom unit is **_em_** or **_rem_**.",
